<title>CHINA: CHINA'S WOOLLEN MILLS IN $52 MLN LOSSES IN 1996.</title>
<headline>CHINA'S WOOLLEN MILLS IN $52 MLN LOSSES IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Losses of China's wool spinning industry reached 430 million yuan ($51.8 million) last year, the Market Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sales of woollen materials last year were down 46.2 percent compared with 1995, it said, quoting the survey by the Ministry of Internal Trade.</p>
<p>Sales in the first quarter of this year were increasing but stockpiles had also risen, up 6.8 percent compared with the same period in 1996, it said.</p>
<p>China has more than 2,400 woollen mills, many of them producing poor quality products with few varieties while demand for woollen worsted of a high quality was huge, it said.</p>
<p>It gave no more details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (86) 10-6532-1921; Fax 6532-4978</p>
